            "title": "Parentheses in literal directory names are now truncated from watch roots",
            "severity": "medium",
            "file": "lib/watcher.js",
            "line": 14,
            "explanation": "The new regex removes any path segment containing an opening parenthesis, even when the parenthesis is part of a literal directory name rather than a glob pattern. For example, configuring a watched file pattern like `/some/x (a|b)/a.js` now yields `/some` as the base directory, so changes under `/some/x (a|b)` will not be watched correctly.",
